# ~/.amux/server.env — mac-server values.
#
# Loaded by amux-server.py at startup via os.environ.setdefault (server.env
# values override process env — see amux-server.py's header comment). Copy
# this file to ~/.amux/server.env and edit; install.sh does this for you only
# if ~/.amux/server.env does not already exist (never clobbers a live config).
# After editing by hand, `touch amux-server.py` to trigger a reload (or wait
# for _watch_server_env's periodic pickup).
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, '#' comments, blank lines ignored. Do NOT
# quote values — this file is parsed by a simple split-on-'=' in
# amux-server.py, not sourced by a shell (unlike defaults.env).

# Model used when a session doesn't request its own --model. Keep in sync
# with defaults.env's CC_DEFAULT_FLAGS if you want the dashboard's "Default"
# label and new-session default to agree.
# AMUX_DEFAULT_MODEL=sonnet

# ── Auto-update: MUST stay unset on mac-server ──────────────────────────────
# This host propagates via deploy/mac-server/amux-pull-update.sh (git pull),
# not the built-in _auto_update_check. That mechanism writes amux-server.py
# wholesale and would desync this checkout from git, breaking the pull-based
# updater it's meant to complement. See docs/mac-server-deploy.md
# "Auto-update" and .omc/plans/mac-server-deploy.md Decision 1.
# AMUX_AUTO_UPDATE_REPO=
# AMUX_AUTO_UPDATE_BRANCH=main
# AMUX_AUTO_UPDATE_INTERVAL=60

# S3 iCal sync — leave unset unless this host also needs a public calendar feed.
# AMUX_S3_BUCKET=
# AMUX_S3_KEY=amux/calendar.ics
# AMUX_S3_REGION=us-east-2

# Disable the git commit-stamp trailer (see MODIFICATIONS.md) if this host's
# sessions shouldn't add an "Amux-Session:" trailer to their commits.
# AMUX_COMMIT_STAMP=1
